### Method Definitions

The `app.get`, `app.post`, `app.all`, and `app.on` methods are defined within the constructor of the `HonoBase` class. The `app.use` method is also defined in this class.

**File:** `src/hono-base.ts`

-   **`app.get`, `app.post`, `app.put`, etc. and `app.all`**: These methods are dynamically created by iterating over a list of HTTP methods.

    ```typescript
    // src/hono-base.ts:125-138
    const allMethods = [...METHODS, METHOD_NAME_ALL_LOWERCASE]
    allMethods.forEach((method) => {
      this[method] = (args1: string | H, ...args: H[]) => {
        if (typeof args1 === 'string') {
          this.#path = args1
        } else {
          this.#addRoute(method, this.#path, args1)
        }
        args.forEach((handler) => {
          this.#addRoute(method, this.#path, handler)
        })
        return this as any
      }
    })
    ```

-   **`app.on`**: This method is explicitly defined to handle routing for one or more HTTP methods and paths.

    ```typescript
    // src/hono-base.ts:141-151
    this.on = (method: string | string[], path: string | string[], ...handlers: H[]) => {
      for (const p of [path].flat()) {
        this.#path = p
        for (const m of [method].flat()) {
          handlers.map((handler) => {
            this.#addRoute(m.toUpperCase(), this.#path, handler)
          })
        }
      }
      return this as any
    }
    ```

-   **`app.use`**: This method is used for adding middleware. It adds a handler that matches all HTTP methods for a given path, effectively calling `addRoute` with the `ALL` method.

